  1. Get Cluster Nodes
kubectl get nodes
Purpose

Shows all worker and control-plane nodes in the cluster.

Example Output
NAME           STATUS   ROLES           AGE   VERSION
master-node    Ready    control-plane   10d   v1.33
worker-node1   Ready    <none>          10d   v1.33
Use Case

Check whether cluster nodes are healthy.

2. Get Pods
kubectl get pods
Purpose

Lists pods in the current namespace.

Example
NAME                     READY   STATUS
nginx-7f4f6d8f4d-kx8jd   1/1     Running
Use Case

Verify if applications are running.

3. Get Pods in All Namespaces
kubectl get pods -A
Purpose

Shows pods from every namespace.

Example
NAMESPACE     NAME                 STATUS
default       nginx-pod            Running
kube-system   coredns              Running
Use Case

Troubleshooting cluster-wide issues.

4. Get Services
kubectl get svc
Purpose

Lists Kubernetes Services.

Example
NAME         TYPE        CLUSTER-IP
kubernetes   ClusterIP   10.96.0.1
nginx-svc    NodePort    10.96.0.20
Use Case

Check application networking.

5. Get Deployments
kubectl get deployments
Purpose

Lists deployments.

Example
NAME    READY   UP-TO-DATE
nginx   3/3     3
Use Case

Verify replica count and deployment status.

6. Describe a Pod
kubectl describe pod nginx-pod
Purpose

Shows detailed pod information.

Information Included
Events
Container status
Image used
Resource limits
Restart count
Use Case
kubectl describe pod mypod

Useful when a pod is failing.

7. View Pod Logs
kubectl logs nginx-pod
Purpose

Displays application logs.

Example
Application Started
Database Connected
Use Case

Debug application issues.

8. Access Pod Terminal
kubectl exec -it nginx-pod -- /bin/bash
Purpose

Log into a running container.

Example
kubectl exec -it nginx-pod -- /bin/sh

Inside pod:

ls
cat file.txt
Use Case

Troubleshooting container issues.

9. Apply YAML File
kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
Purpose

Create or update resources.

Example Deployment
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: nginx
spec:
  replicas: 3
Use Case

Deploy applications.

10. Delete Resources
kubectl delete -f deployment.yaml
Purpose

Deletes resources defined in YAML.

Use Case

Remove deployments, services, etc.

11. Scale Deployment
kubectl scale deployment nginx --replicas=3
Purpose

Increase or decrease pod count.

Before
nginx   1/1
After
nginx   3/3
Use Case

Handle increased traffic.

12. Check Rollout Status
kubectl rollout status deployment/nginx
Purpose

Monitor deployment progress.

Example
deployment "nginx" successfully rolled out
Use Case

Verify deployment success.

13. Rollback Deployment
kubectl rollout undo deployment/nginx
Purpose

Restore previous version.

Example
Rollback to previous deployment
Use Case

Application failure after deployment.

14. View ConfigMaps
kubectl get configmaps
Purpose

Lists configuration data.

Example
NAME
app-config
Use Case

Store environment settings.

15. View Secrets
kubectl get secrets
Purpose

Lists Kubernetes secrets.

Example
NAME
db-password
Use Case

Store passwords and API keys.

16. View Namespaces
kubectl get ns
Purpose

Lists namespaces.

Example
NAME
default
kube-system
dev
prod
Use Case

Environment separation.

17. Node Resource Usage
kubectl top nodes
Purpose

Shows CPU and memory usage.

Example
NAME          CPU(cores)   MEMORY(bytes)
worker-node1  250m         1024Mi
Requirement

Metrics Server must be installed.

18. Pod Resource Usage
kubectl top pods
Purpose

Shows pod resource consumption.

Example
NAME        CPU(cores)   MEMORY
nginx-pod   20m          50Mi
Use Case

Performance monitoring.

19. Get All Resources
kubectl get all
Purpose

Displays:

Pods
Services
Deployments
ReplicaSets
Example
pod/nginx
svc/nginx
deployment/nginx
replicaset/nginx
Use Case

Quick overview of namespace.

20. Cluster Information
kubectl cluster-info
Purpose

Displays cluster endpoints.

Example
Kubernetes control plane is running at https://192.168.1.10:6443
Use Case

Verify cluster connectivity.

